00:40:14.000 --> 00:40:17.000
Hello, you little... ugly thing.

520
00:40:17.000 --> 00:40:20.000
Let's see if you're the one, hmm?

521
00:40:23.000 --> 00:40:26.000
Bend. Morph!

522
00:40:26.000 --> 00:40:27.000
Shape shift.

523
00:40:27.000 --> 00:40:30.000
Well, do something for Odin's sake.

524
00:40:39.000 --> 00:40:42.000
No!

525
00:40:42.000 --> 00:40:46.000
I think it's time to introduce you to man's best friend.

526
00:40:46.000 --> 00:40:49.000
And I don't mean you, Otis.

527
00:40:49.000 --> 00:40:51.000
Okay.

528
00:40:51.000 --> 00:40:53.000
Mommy doesn't want me to do this,

529
00:40:53.000 --> 00:40:56.000
but what Mommy doesn't know won't hurt her.

530
00:40:56.000 --> 00:40:59.000
- ...sour cream and onion... - Oh, look.

531
00:41:03.000 --> 00:41:05.000
Hey, wait a minute.

532
00:41:05.000 --> 00:41:08.000
We don't like your attitude!

533
00:41:08.000 --> 00:41:11.000
Keep an eye on him, will ya?

534
00:41:15.000 --> 00:41:19.000
Look at Bam Bam.

535
00:41:19.000 --> 00:41:21.000
Bam! Bam! Bam! Bam! Bam!

536
00:41:21.000 --> 00:41:26.000
Bam Bam looks miserable without Pebbles.

537
00:41:30.000 --> 00:41:33.000
Bam.

538
00:42:01.000 --> 00:42:05.000
Bam, bam, bam.

539
00:42:50.000 --> 00:42:53.000
Smoking!

540
00:44:44.000 --> 00:44:47.000
I don't know how. I don't know which end is up.

541
00:44:47.000 --> 00:44:49.000
I'm running on fumes.

542
00:44:49.000 --> 00:44:52.000
Yeah. Yeah.

543
00:44:54.000 --> 00:44:57.000
I don't know.

544
00:44:57.000 --> 00:45:00.000
Yeah, I've still got the kid.

545
00:45:00.000 --> 00:45:02.000
Oh God, you have no idea.

546
00:45:02.000 --> 00:45:05.000
Man, they just suck the life out of you.

547
00:45:05.000 --> 00:45:07.000
I don't know what I'm gonna do with him.

548
00:45:07.000 --> 00:45:09.000
I think I may be on to something for my pitch, though.

549
00:45:09.000 --> 00:45:12.000
I don't know, it's just...

550
00:45:39.000 --> 00:45:43.000
Yow! Ooh!

551
00:45:58.000 --> 00:46:01.000
Hi, 911? I already told you.

552
00:46:01.000 --> 00:46:03.000
My son is bouncing off the walls!

553
00:46:03.000 --> 00:46:05.000
Yes, off the walls, the couch,

554
00:46:05.000 --> 00:46:10.000
and the ceiling. Hello. Hello? Hello?!

555
00:46:28.000 --> 00:46:30.000
Don't stop, little...

556
00:46:30.000 --> 00:46:32.000
- Yeah? - Betty!

557
00:46:32.000 --> 00:46:34.000
I need your help.

558
00:46:34.000 --> 00:46:36.000
Tim, what's wrong?

559
00:46:36.000 --> 00:46:38.000
Uh, uh, well, Tonya said if I ever needed...

560
00:46:38.000 --> 00:46:40.000
you know... oh, uh, well, if any... if I saw anything weird.

561
00:46:40.000 --> 00:46:43.000
It's Alvey. It's Alvey. It was Alvey. See?

562
00:46:43.000 --> 00:46:45.000
He was... he was bouncing

563
00:46:45.000 --> 00:46:48.000
and he... he did the Woody laugh, you know...

564
00:46:49.000 --> 00:46:51.000
And he was singing.

565
00:46:51.000 --> 00:46:54.000
Well, lots of babies his age sing.

566
00:46:54.000 --> 00:46:56.000
Vaudeville?

567
00:46:56.000 --> 00:46:58.000
Okay, I'll show you.

568
00:46:58.000 --> 00:47:02.000
Okay, okay. Here we go.

569
00:47:02.000 --> 00:47:06.000
Go on. Sing.

570
00:47:06.000 --> 00:47:10.000
Go on, Alvey.

571
00:47:10.000 --> 00:47:13.000
Do it.

572
00:47:13.000 --> 00:47:16.000
Do it. Sing, damn it!

573
00:47:16.000 --> 00:47:18.000
- Sing... - Tim!

574
00:47:18.000 --> 00:47:21.000
- He's a baby. - Exactly my point.

575
00:47:32.000 --> 00:47:36.000
I'm here to unclog your throne.

576
00:47:39.000 --> 00:47:42.000
Oh, Jason Kemperbee,

577
00:47:42.000 --> 00:47:45.000
be my baby.

578
00:47:45.000 --> 00:47:46.000
Come on.

579
00:47:46.000 --> 00:47:51.000
Hook me up. Show me the magic.

580
00:47:57.000 --> 00:48:00.000
Alvey.

581
00:48:00.000 --> 00:48:01.000
Put that down.

582
00:48:01.000 --> 00:48:04.000
That's Mommy and Daddy's.

583
00:48:04.000 --> 00:48:08.000
Please put the fax machine down.

584
00:48:12.000 --> 00:48:15.000
Want some juice? Here, want some juice?

585
00:48:15.000 --> 00:48:18.000
It's okay. Here you go, Alvey. Have some juice.

586
00:48:18.000 --> 00:48:21.000
Yeah, you like juice.

587
00:48:21.000 --> 00:48:24.000
See, Alvey? Daddy's not gonna hurt you.

588
00:48:24.000 --> 00:48:26.000
Whoa! Hey! Hey! Hey!

589
00:48:26.000 --> 00:48:28.000
No! Hey! Hey! Ah!

590
00:48:28.000 --> 00:48:30.000
Hey! Hey! Hey!

591
00:48:30.000 --> 00:48:35.000
Bam! Bam! Bam! Bam! Bam!

592
00:48:42.000 --> 00:48:45.000
Rattle.

593
00:49:20.000 --> 00:49:23.000
Aww, poor baby.

594
00:49:28.000 --> 00:49:31.000
Huh? Oh!

595
00:49:39.000 --> 00:49:41.000
Uh-oh.

596
00:50:45.000 --> 00:50:46.000
- Yes? - Hi!

597
00:50:46.000 --> 00:50:49.000
Would you like some Thin Chocolate?

598
00:50:57.000 --> 00:51:00.000
Yeah, you can run, but you can't hide!

599
00:51:03.000 --> 00:51:06.000
Transformers.

600
00:51:07.000 --> 00:51:09.000
Alvey?

601
00:51:09.000 --> 00:51:12.000
You... you wouldn't do that to Da-da, would you?

602
00:51:12.000 --> 00:51:14.000
I'm your dad.

603
00:51:14.000 --> 00:51:16.000
C-can you say "dad"?

604
00:51:16.000 --> 00:51:20.000
"Da-da"?

605
00:51:21.000 --> 00:51:24.000
Madre.

606
00:51:25.000 --> 00:51:27.000
This is too much too handle.

607
00:51:27.000 --> 00:51:29.000
I mean, this is insanity.

608
00:51:29.000 --> 00:51:32.000
Dancing?

609
00:51:39.000 --> 00:51:42.000
No. No.

610
00:51:42.000 --> 00:51:46.000
Shh.

611
00:51:54.000 --> 00:51:56.000
Fire!

612
00:51:56.000 --> 00:51:59.000
Bull's-eye!

613
00:52:04.000 --> 00:52:07.000
Hmm?

614
00:52:09.000 --> 00:52:13.000
Here we are by the baby.

615
00:52:34.000 --> 00:52:37.000
Oh, yeah. Who's the dog?

616
00:52:37.000 --> 00:52:40.000
Who's the big dog...

617
00:52:52.000 --> 00:52:56.000
Whoa!

618
00:53:49.000 --> 00:53:52.000
Mommy!

619
00:54:23.000 --> 00:54:26.000
I surrender.

620
00:54:42.000 --> 00:54:44.000
Bye-bye.

621
00:54:56.000 --> 00:54:59.000
Oh, shoot.

622
00:55:03.000 --> 00:55:06.000
Oh!

623
00:55:12.000 --> 00:55:13.000
Stop it!

624
00:55:13.000 --> 00:55:16.000
This is insane!

625
00:55:16.000 --> 00:55:19.000
Point it down!

626
00:55:24.000 --> 00:55:28.000
- All done? - Hmm.

627
00:55:46.000 --> 00:55:48.000
- Hey, I'm Rod. - Get in here!

628
00:55:48.000 --> 00:55:50.000
Okay.

629
00:55:50.000 --> 00:55:53.000
Uh, take a look at this.

630
00:55:53.000 --> 00:55:56.000
Hey, what a cute little baby.

631
00:55:56.000 --> 00:55:58.000
- Oh, of course! - Mind if I take a look at him?

632
00:55:58.000 --> 00:56:01.000
No, go ahead. I don't care.

633
00:56:01.000 --> 00:56:03.000
Come on. Do something crazy.

634
00:56:03.000 --> 00:56:05.000
Yeah, do something crazy!

635
00:56:05.000 --> 00:56:08.000
Crap! Huh-uh, huh-uh.

636
00:56:08.000 --> 00:56:11.000
Damn it. This isn't the right one either.

637
00:56:12.000 --> 00:56:14.000
Hey! What are you doing?

638
00:56:14.000 --> 00:56:17.000
Uh, I left your package in the foyer.

639
00:56:21.000 --> 00:56:24.000
Do I have a package? Okay.

640
00:56:29.000 --> 00:56:34.000
Oh well.

641
00:56:36.000 --> 00:56:39.000
What happened?

642
00:56:40.000 --> 00:56:44.000
You did this to me. I know what you're doing.

643
00:56:44.000 --> 00:56:46.000
You're trying to drive me crazy.

644
00:56:46.000 --> 00:56:48.000
You're a cunning little mastermind

645
00:56:48.000 --> 00:56:51.000
who will stop at nothing until I go

646
00:56:51.000 --> 00:56:54.000
completely insane.

647
00:56:55.000 --> 00:56:57.000
Well, come on.

648
00:56:57.000 --> 00:57:00.000
Start dancing again.

649
00:57:00.000 --> 00:57:04.000
Start screwing with my mind!

650
00:57:04.000 --> 00:57:07.000
Start, huh? Come on!

651
00:57:11.000 --> 00:57:14.000
Why aren't you screwing with my mind?

652
00:57:17.000 --> 00:57:26.000
Maybe I am just going crazy.

653
00:57:26.000 --> 00:57:31.000
Maybe I am just going...

654
00:57:48.000 --> 00:57:51.000
That's it, buddy. First I'm taking you to a pediatrician,

655
00:57:51.000 --> 00:57:54.000
then I'm taking you to an exorcist.

656
00:58:03.000 --> 00:58:06.000
Who are you?!

657
00:58:06.000 --> 00:58:08.000
Oh my G...

658
00:58:08.000 --> 00:58:11.000
my son is the devil. My son is the devil.

659
00:58:11.000 --> 00:58:15.000
Oh my Odin, it is him.

660
00:58:17.000 --> 00:58:19.000
We're just going to have a nice little drive,

661
00:58:19.000 --> 00:58:22.000
while Daddy has a nervous breakdown.

662
00:58:23.000 --> 00:58:25.000
Please leave a message.

663
00:58:25.000 --> 00:58:28.000
Tonya, it's Betty. You said I should keep an eye out

664
00:58:28.000 --> 00:58:30.000
and call you if there are any problems?

665
00:58:30.000 --> 00:58:32.000
I think there's a problem.

666
00:58:46.000 --> 00:58:48.000
No parking there.

667
00:58:48.000 --> 00:58:51.000
That's a handicapped zone!

668
00:58:51.000 --> 00:58:54.000
Hey! Sir?

669
00:58:58.000 --> 00:59:00.000
Hey, wait!

670
00:59:00.000 --> 00:59:03.000
Stop! You!

671
00:59:03.000 --> 00:59:07.000
Hey!

672
00:59:08.000 --> 00:59:11.000
What is it?

673
00:59:11.000 --> 00:59:13.000
- Ah! - Okay, where is the mask?

674
00:59:13.000 --> 00:59:15.000
- What? - The mask. My mask. Where is it?

675
00:59:15.000 --> 00:59:17.000
What are you talking about? Who are you?

676
00:59:17.000 --> 00:59:19.000
I am Loki, God of Mischief.

677
00:59:19.000 --> 00:59:22.000
Yeah, and I'm Tim, God of Crazy Babyland. Will you get out of the way?

678
00:59:22.000 --> 00:59:23.000
That baby is born of the mask... my mask.

679
00:59:23.000 --> 00:59:26.000
- Now, where is it?! - Born of the mask... what?

680
00:59:27.000 --> 00:59:31.000
Oh, so that explains why he could pee like that!

681
00:59:31.000 --> 00:59:34.000
But wait a minute. This is my baby.

682
00:59:34.000 --> 00:59:36.000
I don't care about that. Just give me my mask!

683
00:59:36.000 --> 00:59:38.000
- I don't know where it is. - Oh really?

684
00:59:38.000 --> 00:59:41.000
Maybe this will jog your memory!

685
00:59:44.000 --> 00:59:47.000
- Loki!! - Dad?!

686
00:59:47.000 --> 00:59:49.000
I've warned you! You've left me no other choice.

687
00:59:49.000 --> 00:59:53.000
I don't have time for this. Look, Dad, there's Balder.

688
01:00:19.000 --> 01:00:23.000
- Just give me the mask. - I don't have it.

689
01:00:24.000 --> 01:00:26.000
I think my dog ate it.

690
01:00:26.000 --> 01:00:29.000
That is the oldest excuse in the book,

691
01:00:29.000 --> 01:00:32.000
and I've read some really, really old books.

692
01:00:32.000 --> 01:00:36.000
But if you want to do this the hard way...

693
01:00:36.000 --> 01:00:39.000
so be it.

694
01:00:59.000 --> 01:01:02.000
Oh, you're good.

695
01:01:05.000 --> 01:01:08.000
- Whoa. - Yeah.

696
01:01:11.000 --> 01:01:13.000
You really are a chip off the old block.

697
01:01:13.000 --> 01:01:18.000
But I don't have time for this. Prepare to feel my true power!

698
01:01:27.000 --> 01:01:32.000
Loki!

699
01:01:35.000 --> 01:01:37.000
You have defied me

700
01:01:37.000 --> 01:01:40.000
for the last time.

701
01:01:40.000 --> 01:01:41.000
I've had it up to here with you!

702
01:01:41.000 --> 01:01:44.000
Dad, please listen to me. You're holding the baby.

703
01:01:44.000 --> 01:01:49.000
Silence! You have left me no choice.

704
01:01:49.000 --> 01:01:51.000
- Listen, listen... - You are hereby stripped

705
01:01:51.000 --> 01:01:54.000
of your immortal powers and forever banished

706
01:01:54.000 --> 01:01:56.000
to the land of mortals.

707
01:01:56.000 --> 01:02:00.000
No! Please, hear me out. That baby...

708
01:02:11.000 --> 01:02:14.000
Whoa.

709
01:02:31.000 --> 01:02:33.000
- Pretty. - Whoa.

710
01:02:33.000 --> 01:02:38.000
Whoa.

711
01:02:39.000 --> 01:02:41.000
- Hello? - Where the hell are you, homes?

712
01:02:41.000 --> 01:02:44.000
Your pitch meeting is starting right now.

713
01:02:44.000 --> 01:02:46.000
Um, I just met Green.

714
01:02:46.000 --> 01:02:49.000
- Loki. - Snap out of it.

715
01:02:49.000 --> 01:02:52.000
Where are you? I'll pick you up.

716
01:02:56.000 --> 01:02:59.000
What's the deal, Tim? I get you a network pitch,

717
01:02:59.000 --> 01:03:01.000
and you repay me by showing up 20 minutes late

718
01:03:01.000 --> 01:03:03.000
looking like an escaped mental patient?

719
01:03:03.000 --> 01:03:05.000
Andwith a kid?

720
01:03:05.000 --> 01:03:07.000
Huh?

721
01:03:07.000 --> 01:03:09.000
This is Tim Avery.

722
01:03:09.000 --> 01:03:11.000
He created the character,

723
01:03:11.000 --> 01:03:14.000
so why don't I just let him tell you more about it?

724
01:03:14.000 --> 01:03:16.000
Tim?

725
01:03:22.000 --> 01:03:25.000
Tim?

726
01:03:28.000 --> 01:03:30.000
Guys, I could walk.

727
01:03:30.000 --> 01:03:33.000
I-I guess he didn't like the pitch.

728
01:03:33.000 --> 01:03:38.000
I just... I wanna get all my stuff.

729
01:03:38.000 --> 01:03:40.000
Tim?

730
01:03:40.000 --> 01:03:42.000
Pick up the phone!

731
01:03:42.000 --> 01:03:44.000
Tim!

732
01:03:44.000 --> 01:03:47.000
Betty just called. She's completely freaked out!

733
01:03:47.000 --> 01:03:51.000
Oh, God. Call me the second you get this message.

734
01:03:55.000 --> 01:03:57.000
Hey, it's me.

735
01:03:57.000 --> 01:03:59.000
Uh, got your message.

736
01:03:59.000 --> 01:04:01.000
Well, things are really great here.

737
01:04:01.000 --> 01:04:05.000
Uh, me and Alvey got chased by a guy named Loki.

738
01:04:05.000 --> 01:04:08.000
Well, that's not important.

739
01:04:08.000 --> 01:04:11.000
I pitched, uh, my show today,

740
01:04:11.000 --> 01:04:13.000
and, um...

741
01:04:13.000 --> 01:04:16.000
I got fired.

742
01:04:18.000 --> 01:04:20.000
Yeah.

743
01:04:20.000 --> 01:04:22.000
Um...

744
01:04:22.000 --> 01:04:24.000
but Alvey pooped,

745
01:04:24.000 --> 01:04:27.000
which is good, and, uh...

746
01:04:28.000 --> 01:04:31.000
and Alvey saved me.

747
01:04:31.000 --> 01:04:34.000
It was amazing.

748
01:04:34.000 --> 01:04:36.000
But, uh, uh, the main thing is, uh,

749
01:04:36.000 --> 01:04:38.000
we're totally fine. Everything's great.

750
01:04:38.000 --> 01:04:41.000
Um, better than fine, actually.

751
01:04:41.000 --> 01:04:43.000
Alvey's great.

752
01:04:43.000 --> 01:04:45.000
I love you.

753
01:04:45.000 --> 01:04:48.000
Okay, bye.

754
01:06:22.000 --> 01:06:25.000
Whoa!

755
01:06:54.000 --> 01:06:58.000
By Kylvie, King of Svitjod,

756
01:06:58.000 --> 01:07:02.000
Houthedy and Yppor.

757
01:07:02.000 --> 01:07:06.000
I summon thee, God of Gunningap

758
01:07:06.000 --> 01:07:09.000
- Nifleheim, Kvelge... - Tim?

759
01:07:12.000 --> 01:07:15.000
Tim? Is that you?

760
01:07:15.000 --> 01:07:17.000
Tim!

761
01:07:21.000 --> 01:07:26.000
Kvelgemir!

762
01:07:34.000 --> 01:07:36.000
Who summons Odin,

763
01:07:36.000 --> 01:07:39.000
- Allfather of the gods? - Shh!

764
01:07:39.000 --> 01:07:41.000
- G... Loki?! - Shh!

765
01:07:41.000 --> 01:07:43.000
- You'll wake the baby. - Oh, sorry.

766
01:07:43.000 --> 01:07:47.000
Loki, is that you?

767
01:07:47.000 --> 01:07:48.000
Tim.

768
01:07:48.000 --> 01:07:50.000
What are you doing in there?

769
01:07:50.000 --> 01:07:52.000
You did the conjuring ceremony

770
01:07:52.000 --> 01:07:54.000
- by yourself? - I pay attention.

771
01:07:54.000 --> 01:07:57.000
- Sometimes. - But you don't have the mask.

772
01:07:57.000 --> 01:08:00.000
- Well, yeah, that's why I... - Rules are rules, Loki!!

773
01:08:00.000 --> 01:08:02.000
And I specifically... ow!

774
01:08:02.000 --> 01:08:06.000
Could you just stop lecturing me for one minute and listen?!

775
01:08:06.000 --> 01:08:09.000
I found the baby. He's right there.

776
01:08:09.000 --> 01:08:12.000
- That child is strong. - Mmm.

777
01:08:13.000 --> 01:08:15.000
Very strong.

778
01:08:15.000 --> 01:08:18.000
I had him before. I was this close,

779
01:08:18.000 --> 01:08:20.000
but you took my powers and they got away.

780
01:08:20.000 --> 01:08:22.000
So, please, father,

781
01:08:22.000 --> 01:08:24.000
give me my powers

782
01:08:24.000 --> 01:08:28.000
and I will give you the mask.

783
01:08:31.000 --> 01:08:33.000
Very well.

784
01:08:33.000 --> 01:08:35.000
Your resourcefulness pleases me,

785
01:08:35.000 --> 01:08:38.000
and your mother says we should be trying

786
01:08:38.000 --> 01:08:40.000
"positive reinforcement,"

787
01:08:40.000 --> 01:08:42.000
whatever the Helveti that is.

788
01:08:42.000 --> 01:08:45.000
So, as a reward,

789
01:08:45.000 --> 01:08:48.000
I shall grant you a reprieve.

790
01:08:48.000 --> 01:08:52.000
You have until the sands have fallen.

791
01:08:52.000 --> 01:08:54.000
Oh, hey, hey. Wait, wait. Hang on.

792
01:08:54.000 --> 01:08:55.000
- Hmm? - I want to sync up.

793
01:08:55.000 --> 01:08:59.000
Ready... now!

794
01:09:00.000 --> 01:09:03.000
Don't disappoint me, Loki. Use your powers wisely

795
01:09:03.000 --> 01:09:06.000
and complete your task. This truly is

796
01:09:06.000 --> 01:09:09.000
your final chance!

797
01:09:31.000 --> 01:09:33.000
Tim.

798
01:09:33.000 --> 01:09:36.000
What's going on up there?

799
01:09:37.000 --> 01:09:40.000
Tim Avery, what are you doing in there?

800
01:09:42.000 --> 01:09:46.000
Hmm. Nosy neighbors.

801
01:09:46.000 --> 01:09:50.000
Ah... ah... choo!

802
01:10:08.000 --> 01:10:11.000
- Guess who? - No! Ah!

803
01:10:12.000 --> 01:10:14.000
Tim, snap out of it!

804
01:10:14.000 --> 01:10:16.000
Baby?

805
01:10:16.000 --> 01:10:19.000
- Is that you? - Of course it's me.

806
01:10:19.000 --> 01:10:21.000
What are you doing up so late?

807
01:10:21.000 --> 01:10:24.000
- And where's Alvey? - Seriously.

808
01:10:24.000 --> 01:10:26.000
Is that really you?

809
01:10:26.000 --> 01:10:28.000
No, you idiot.

810
01:10:28.000 --> 01:10:32.000
Oh God. Ah... what... I...

811
01:10:34.000 --> 01:10:36.000
Oh Jeez.

812
01:10:36.000 --> 01:10:38.000
Bro, listen.

813
01:10:38.000 --> 01:10:41.000
I'm a god. I can shape shift.

814
01:10:41.000 --> 01:10:43.000
I can create stuff out of nothingness.

815
01:10:43.000 --> 01:10:45.000
I can alter the fabric of reality,

816
01:10:45.000 --> 01:10:49.000
so, please, quit being a knucklehead.

817
01:10:49.000 --> 01:10:52.000
- What do you want from us? - Oh, don't worry.

818
01:10:52.000 --> 01:10:54.000
I'm not gonna hurt you...

819
01:10:54.000 --> 01:10:56.000
yet!

820
01:10:56.000 --> 01:10:58.000
This baby was born out of the mask,

821
01:10:58.000 --> 01:11:01.000
and I want my mask back!

822
01:11:01.000 --> 01:11:04.000
Meet me in exactly one hour.

823
01:11:08.000 --> 01:11:12.000
So you find the mask and meet me at... hmm.

824
01:11:12.000 --> 01:11:15.000
Where shall we meet? Um, how about Red Lobster?

825
01:11:15.000 --> 01:11:18.000
It's always so difficult getting a table there, especially on Fridays

826
01:11:18.000 --> 01:11:20.000
- when they do that special. - There's a wick burning.

827
01:11:20.000 --> 01:11:22.000
Well, how about we meet in an alley in the city?

828
01:11:22.000 --> 01:11:24.000
- There's a wick... - Met at one before.

829
01:11:24.000 --> 01:11:26.000
- Sure, it's a little cliche... - Sir, your...

830
01:11:26.000 --> 01:11:29.000
but it's not so cliche that I think to myself, "Wow, that's too cliche!"

831
01:11:29.000 --> 01:11:32.000
- But... it... it... - Meet me in that alley within the hour,

832
01:11:32.000 --> 01:11:34.000
with the mask,

833
01:11:34.000 --> 01:11:38.000
if you ever want to see your little monster again.

834
01:11:38.000 --> 01:11:41.000
No!

835
01:11:43.000 --> 01:11:47.000
Alvey! No!

836
01:12:02.000 --> 01:12:06.000
What... Tim?

837
01:12:07.000 --> 01:12:09.000
Tim?!

838
01:12:09.000 --> 01:12:12.000
Alvey?!

839
01:12:13.000 --> 01:12:15.000
Oh God. Tim!

840
01:12:15.000 --> 01:12:18.000
What are you... what are you...

841
01:12:19.000 --> 01:12:21.000
Tim. What are you doing?

842
01:12:21.000 --> 01:12:24.000
What are you doing?

843
01:12:27.000 --> 01:12:30.000
What the hell is wrong with you?! Get off of me!

844
01:12:30.000 --> 01:12:34.000
Get out of there, Loki! Where's my son, you mongrel from hell?

845
01:12:41.000 --> 01:12:43.000
Tim! Ah!

846
01:12:43.000 --> 01:12:46.000
Tonya?!

847
01:12:48.000 --> 01:12:51.000
Tonya! Oh, it's really you.

848
01:12:51.000 --> 01:12:54.000
- Oh my God. - Oh God, I'm so sorry.

849
01:12:54.000 --> 01:12:56.000
Betty was right. You have gone crazy.

850
01:12:56.000 --> 01:13:00.000
No, I haven't. I thought I did, but I didn't.

851
01:13:01.000 --> 01:13:04.000
Where's Alvey?

852
01:13:04.000 --> 01:13:06.000
- Okay, don't freak out. - Where's Alvey?!

853
01:13:06.000 --> 01:13:08.000
- You're freaking out. - Where's my baby?!

854
01:13:08.000 --> 01:13:10.000
- Loki t-took him. - Took him?!

855
01:13:10.000 --> 01:13:12.000
Oh my God. Did you call the police?!

856
01:13:12.000 --> 01:13:15.000
- No, I... - Oh my God.

857
01:13:15.000 --> 01:13:17.000
Tonya, listen!

858
01:13:17.000 --> 01:13:19.000
- This is an emergency! - Tonya!!

859
01:13:19.000 --> 01:13:22.000
- My son is missing... - No, Tonya, listen!

860
01:13:22.000 --> 01:13:25.000
The police can't help us! He's the freaking God of Mischief.

861
01:13:25.000 --> 01:13:28.000
All he wants is his mask, which Otis is wearing.

862
01:13:28.000 --> 01:13:31.000
And if I can just figure out where Otis is, I can just...

863
01:13:31.000 --> 01:13:33.000
of course!

864
01:13:33.000 --> 01:13:37.000
Our child is missing and you're worried about the damned dog?!

865
01:13:37.000 --> 01:13:39.000
This is crazy!

866
01:13:39.000 --> 01:13:40.000
See what I'm talking about?

867
01:13:40.000 --> 01:13:42.000
Now, you're gonna have to trust me

868
01:13:42.000 --> 01:13:46.000
and get in the car, because I know where Alvey is and I know how to get him back,

869
01:13:46.000 --> 01:13:49.000
because I know the one place Otis the moose would go.

870
01:14:02.000 --> 01:14:04.000
See there's this really cute pooch Venus.

871
01:14:04.000 --> 01:14:06.000
Otis?

872
01:14:06.000 --> 01:14:08.000
Otis!

873
01:14:08.000 --> 01:14:11.000
That's not Otis! That's a green critter.

874
01:14:11.000 --> 01:14:13.000
I'm sorry, okay?

875
01:14:13.000 --> 01:14:16.000
I've ignored you and I've been impatient,

876
01:14:16.000 --> 01:14:19.000
but I need you, buddy. Loki, that guy that made the mask?

877
01:14:19.000 --> 01:14:21.000
He wants it back. He has Alvey.

878
01:14:21.000 --> 01:14:23.000
And he's a bad guy, Otis.

879
01:14:23.000 --> 01:14:25.000
He hates dogs.

880
01:14:25.000 --> 01:14:28.000
He doesn't realize that dogs are truly man's best friend.

881
01:14:28.000 --> 01:14:30.000
- Huh? - You heard me.

882
01:14:30.000 --> 01:14:32.000
You're this man's best friend.

883
01:14:32.000 --> 01:14:35.000
But Alvey's my son

884
01:14:35.000 --> 01:14:38.000
which sort of makes you like his big brother.

885
01:14:38.000 --> 01:14:42.000
And when he grows up, he's gonna be your bestest friend.

886
01:14:42.000 --> 01:14:44.000
But right now, he needs you

887
01:14:44.000 --> 01:14:48.000
and he needs that mask.

888
01:14:51.000 --> 01:14:54.000
All right.

889
01:15:01.000 --> 01:15:03.000
So, I guess you're

890
01:15:03.000 --> 01:15:06.000
kinda cute, huh?

891
01:15:07.000 --> 01:15:09.000
Um, can you, like,

892
01:15:09.000 --> 01:15:11.000
do anything you want, like me?

893
01:15:11.000 --> 01:15:14.000
I mean, can you do this?

894
01:15:19.000 --> 01:15:21.000
Wow.

895
01:15:21.000 --> 01:15:23.000
Well, look at you!

896
01:15:23.000 --> 01:15:26.000
You're just a little outlaw, ain't you?

897
01:15:33.000 --> 01:15:38.000
Okay, hombre. Let's see how tough your rawhide can be.

898
01:15:55.000 --> 01:15:58.000
Gotcha.

899
01:16:02.000 --> 01:16:05.000
I like it!

900
01:16:05.000 --> 01:16:07.000
So, you like games, huh?

901
01:16:07.000 --> 01:16:09.000
Well you'd better watch out

902
01:16:09.000 --> 01:16:13.000
'cause I've got a game that no one can beat me at.

903
01:16:14.000 --> 01:16:17.000
Super Twister!

904
01:16:18.000 --> 01:16:20.000
It's just around the corner, right here.

905
01:16:20.000 --> 01:16:23.000
Here we go.

906
01:16:34.000 --> 01:16:37.000
Isn't this fun?

907
01:17:04.000 --> 01:17:09.000
Whoa!

908
01:17:12.000 --> 01:17:16.000
No fair! That crash threw me. Rematch!

909
01:17:24.000 --> 01:17:26.000
Okay, you give me Alvey,

910
01:17:26.000 --> 01:17:29.000
and the mask is yours.

911
01:17:45.000 --> 01:17:47.000
I can't let go. I've grown attached.

912
01:17:47.000 --> 01:17:49.000
- Alvey! - Hey, we had a deal!

913
01:17:49.000 --> 01:17:53.000
I'm the God of friggin' Mischief, what did you expect?

914
01:18:25.000 --> 01:18:27.000
- Huh. - Hey, Loki.

915
01:18:27.000 --> 01:18:30.000
Honey, you look hot.

916
01:18:30.000 --> 01:18:32.000
Give me back my son!

917
01:18:32.000 --> 01:18:35.000
Um... no.

918
01:18:37.000 --> 01:18:40.000
Honey, I think it's time we trade up.

919
01:18:58.000 --> 01:19:00.000
Buckle up, baby.

920
01:19:08.000 --> 01:19:10.000
Listen to Loki, kid.

921
01:19:10.000 --> 01:19:14.000
Dads are overrated and I speak from experience.

922
01:19:15.000 --> 01:19:19.000
Ah, there's nothing like a Sunday drive.

923
01:19:20.000 --> 01:19:23.000
You wanna have some fun, kid, you stick with me.

924
01:19:35.000 --> 01:19:39.000
All right. It's time to lose them for good.

925
01:19:46.000 --> 01:19:49.000
Oh, look out, look out, look out!

926
01:19:50.000 --> 01:19:52.000
Yahoo!

927
01:20:00.000 --> 01:20:03.000
Whoa!!

928
01:20:03.000 --> 01:20:07.000
Hey, babe, look. No hands. I'm kidding.

929
01:20:07.000 --> 01:20:09.000
Let's just finish this.

930
01:20:12.000 --> 01:20:16.000
Now, where did he go?

931
01:20:16.000 --> 01:20:18.000
- Hmm. - Uh, honey?

932
01:20:18.000 --> 01:20:21.000
I think, maybe, there?

933
01:20:35.000 --> 01:20:38.000
And here he is, folks,

934
01:20:38.000 --> 01:20:42.000
the failure of Fringe City,

935
01:20:42.000 --> 01:20:47.000
Yes, it's Tim "No-win" Avery!

936
01:20:47.000 --> 01:20:50.000
Tim, it's Alvey. I'm gonna go get him.

937
01:20:50.000 --> 01:20:53.000
Kick his can, honey.

938
01:21:06.000 --> 01:21:10.000
Float like a butterfly, sting like a bee.

939
01:21:12.000 --> 01:21:14.000
Hi, baby. Hi, baby. Hi, baby.

940
01:21:14.000 --> 01:21:18.000
Oh, yeah? Well, jump like a grasshopper

941
01:21:18.000 --> 01:21:21.000
and stink like a skunk!

942
01:21:22.000 --> 01:21:24.000
Caught me with my mouth open!

943
01:21:24.000 --> 01:21:26.000
You can't fight me if you're locked in a trunk.

944
01:21:26.000 --> 01:21:29.000
Huh?

945
01:21:32.000 --> 01:21:36.000
I'm coming, I'm coming.

946
01:21:45.000 --> 01:21:48.000
Let's get out of this dump. Come on.

947
01:21:48.000 --> 01:21:51.000
And Loki said, "Let there be a brick wall!"

948
01:21:51.000 --> 01:21:55.000
And there was!

949
01:21:55.000 --> 01:21:57.000
Okay!

950
01:21:57.000 --> 01:22:01.000
No more Mr. Nice Guy!

951
01:22:02.000 --> 01:22:06.000
Say hello to my little friend!

952
01:22:12.000 --> 01:22:15.000
Tim! Tim!

953
01:22:21.000 --> 01:22:24.000
Here's Loki!

954
01:22:27.000 --> 01:22:30.000
Tim, Tim, Tim, Tim, T-T-T-T-T...

955
01:22:42.000 --> 01:22:44.000
Wait.

956
01:22:44.000 --> 01:22:45.000
This is a waste of time.

957
01:22:45.000 --> 01:22:49.000
We're evenly-matched opponents.

958
01:22:50.000 --> 01:22:53.000
I think we should let the kid decide.

959
01:22:53.000 --> 01:22:56.000
Why, that's a swell idea.

960
01:23:02.000 --> 01:23:06.000
Alvey, this is your decision.

961
01:23:06.000 --> 01:23:09.000
- Pick me, pick me! - Alvey?

962
01:23:09.000 --> 01:23:14.000
- I'm your real dad! - Come on, you little devil. Let's play!

963
01:23:14.000 --> 01:23:18.000
- Come on, Alvey. - Alvey.

964
01:23:23.000 --> 01:23:24.000
Alvey?

965
01:23:24.000 --> 01:23:27.000
- Yeah, that's right. - Tim!

966
01:23:27.000 --> 01:23:31.000
Son.

967
01:23:45.000 --> 01:23:48.000
Alvey, look at me.

968
01:23:48.000 --> 01:23:51.000
It's your dad.

969
01:23:51.000 --> 01:23:54.000
There's no more superpowers.

970
01:23:54.000 --> 01:23:57.000
I know at first I was kind of a jerk.

971
01:23:58.000 --> 01:24:00.000
I didn't know how to handle a son,

972
01:24:00.000 --> 01:24:03.000
but you helped me grow up.

973
01:24:03.000 --> 01:24:05.000
And I want to repay you

974
01:24:05.000 --> 01:24:08.000
by helping you grow up.

975
01:24:09.000 --> 01:24:12.000
I love you.

976
01:24:14.000 --> 01:24:18.000
Come on.

977
01:24:21.000 --> 01:24:24.000
- Da-da. - Oh, Alvey.

978
01:24:24.000 --> 01:24:27.000
It's my son.

979
01:24:29.000 --> 01:24:32.000
Yes.

980
01:24:34.000 --> 01:24:38.000
I just wanted a friend.

981
01:25:22.000 --> 01:25:25.000
Push! Push!

982
01:25:39.000 --> 01:25:41.000
Huh?

983
01:26:14.000 --> 01:26:18.000
Off the throne. He's off the throne. That's not good.

984
01:26:18.000 --> 01:26:20.000
Your time is up, son.

985
01:26:20.000 --> 01:26:23.000
As expected, you failed in your promise.

986
01:26:23.000 --> 01:26:25.000
You failed in your quest.

987
01:26:25.000 --> 01:26:29.000
You are, in every sense of the word,

988
01:26:29.000 --> 01:26:32.000
- a failure. - And I thought your dad was mean.

989
01:26:32.000 --> 01:26:34.000
Hey, we both knew it would end like this, right?

990
01:26:34.000 --> 01:26:37.000
You always set me up to fail. At least in that respect,

991
01:26:37.000 --> 01:26:39.000
- I'm living up to your expectations. - Silence!

992
01:26:39.000 --> 01:26:43.000
You've brought me much pain, Loki.

993
01:26:44.000 --> 01:26:48.000
Right back at you, Dad.

994
01:26:48.000 --> 01:26:49.000
- Hey! - Tim, no!

995
01:26:49.000 --> 01:26:52.000
Hang on just a minute, Grizzly Adams.

996
01:26:52.000 --> 01:26:54.000
I don't know how things work in the god world,

997
01:26:54.000 --> 01:26:58.000
but you're his father, he's your son.

998
01:26:58.000 --> 01:27:02.000
And even if you banish him, he's still gonna be your son.

999
01:27:03.000 --> 01:27:07.000
There is nothing more important in this entire universe

1000
01:27:07.000 --> 01:27:09.000
than your relationship with your family,

1001
01:27:09.000 --> 01:27:11.000
especially if you're immortal.

1002
01:27:11.000 --> 01:27:14.000
You're like 1,000, he's like 800,

1003
01:27:14.000 --> 01:27:15.000
so you might as well get things right now

1004
01:27:15.000 --> 01:27:19.000
and enjoy the rest of your eternal life.

1005
01:27:19.000 --> 01:27:23.000
Here's the thing. Just take it.

1006
01:27:26.000 --> 01:27:30.000
Okay? Loosen up.

1007
01:27:44.000 --> 01:27:47.000
Come on, son. Let's go home.

1008
01:27:47.000 --> 01:27:50.000
- Okay? - Okay.

1009
01:27:50.000 --> 01:27:53.000
Godspeed.

1010
01:27:57.000 --> 01:28:00.000
Maybe now, I can help you patch things up with Mom?

1011
01:28:00.000 --> 01:28:03.000
Don't push it.

1012
01:28:18.000 --> 01:28:21.000
A baby and a dog competing for Dad's attention...

1013
01:28:21.000 --> 01:28:23.000
I love it.

1014
01:28:23.000 --> 01:28:27.000
Simple, but it's... it's got...

1015
01:28:27.000 --> 01:28:30.000
- Spark? - Yes.

1016
01:28:30.000 --> 01:28:32.000
Where did you get the idea?

1017
01:28:32.000 --> 01:28:38.000
Well, I just kind of quit trying so hard and...

1018
01:28:40.000 --> 01:28:42.000
the idea just came to me.

1019
01:28:42.000 --> 01:28:45.000
It's great.

1020
01:29:14.000 --> 01:29:16.000
Yay! Yay!

1021
01:29:16.000 --> 01:29:19.000
Honey, oh.

1022
01:29:19.000 --> 01:29:22.000
That was such a good show!

1023
01:29:22.000 --> 01:29:25.000
But I think you might need to add another character.

1024
01:29:25.000 --> 01:29:28.000
What?

1025
01:29:31.000 --> 01:29:34.000
- Really? - Yeah.

1026
01:29:37.000 --> 01:29:40.000
What do you think about that, Double A?

1027
01:29:40.000 --> 01:29:42.000
A little brother or sister?

1028
01:29:42.000 --> 01:29:45.000
How does that sound?

